-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",442,{
[14113]="7005986F\n1\tPlace jars along the road to the Bonfire Glade (total: 5)\tThe road to the Bonfire Glade lies just beyond the Old Forest Tunnel on the eastern border of Buckland. Shirriff Hob Hayward has asked you to set up jars of foul-smelling brew along the road to ward off aggressive wildlife.\n2\tTalk to Hob Hayward\tShirriff Hob Hayward is guarding the Buckland Gate in Buckland. You should let him know that you've set up the jars in the Old Forest.\n",
[14114]="700479E0\n1\tTalk to Mírthel\tMírthel can be found at Haerondir. You should talk to Mírthel.\n2\tTravel to the small Ranger outpost in the Slag-hills\tA small ranger outpost is hidden in the Slag-hills. You should find Candúr in the Ranger outpost hidden by the Slag-hills.\n3\tTalk to Candúr\tCandúr can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills. You should talk to Candúr and hear his message.\n4\tTalk to Thurindol\tThurindol can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills. You should talk to Thurindol.\n",
[14115]="700078A0\n1\tBring the lockbox to Constable Sageford\030Collect the Blackwold lockbox\tThe Blackwolds have many camps along the road east and north of Combe. Constable Sageford is in Combe. Constable Sageford wants you to recover a brigand lockbox from one of the watch-fires in the Chetwood. Its contents can then be used to reimburse those who lost property to the Blackwold.\n",
[14116]="7003FFEC\n1\tSearch cocoons in Lhingroth for missing Gondorians (total: 8)\tCocoons can be found inside Lhingroth, slightly east of Sardol in southern Blackroot Vale. Sidharan has asked you to brave the spiders of Lhingroth in hopes of finding people that have gone missing from Sardol in recent days.\n2\tTalk to Sidharan\tSidharan can be found in Sardol in south-western Blackroot Vale. You have searched all of the cocoons you could find in Lhingroth and rescued a few inhabitants of Sardol. You should return to Sidharan with this news.\n",
[14117]="700622EE\n1\tDefeat wood-trolls in Tham Lasgol (total: 12)\tTham Lasgol can be found west of Idhobel. Rhovandis has asked you to defeat wood-trolls at Tham Lasgol.\n2\tTalk to Rhovandis\tYou found and defeated wood-troll intruders at Tham Lasgol. You should tell Rhovandis about the new inhabitants. Return to Rhovandis.\n",
[14118]="70068655\n1\tTalk to Zemirah at the Sailors' Guild-hall\030Talk to Ahûd at the northern shipyard\030Examine Râmax\030Talk to Râmax at the southern shipyard\tZemirah is at the Sailors' Guild-hall, Ahûd is at the northern shipyard, and Râmax is at the southern shipyard. Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, wants to assess the threat of the Heirsworn following the Sea-stone Mutiny.\n2\tTalk to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower\tEshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. You have spoken to Zemirah and Ahûd, but Râmax was slain by the Heirsworn in the Sail-haven. You should report to Eshmun.\n",
[14119]="7005F86B\n1\tTalk to Hersegg at Zâram-mekhem\tHersegg can be found at Zâram-mekhem in Gloomingtarn. Spall hopes to join Lord Hermáth Stormhammer's expedition at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. You should talk to Hersegg on his behalf.\n2\tAid Hersegg with 'Gorgar's Curse-breaker'\030Aid Spall with 'Echoes of the Ancestors'\tHersegg and Spall can be found at Zâram-mekhem in Gloomingtarn. In exchange for your aid in combating the Orkish presence in Gloomingtarn, Hersegg has indicated that she is willing to escort Spall to Watchers' Roost. You should aid Hersegg and Spall.\n3\tFollow the thoroughfare through Gloomingtarn and travel to Watchers' Roost\tWatchers' Roost can be found in Gloomingtarn, along the thoroughfare between the Deepscrave and the Clovengap. After hindering the Orcs encamped at Drúkala, Hersegg told you to join the rest of her grandfather's expedition at Watchers' Roost. You should travel to Watchers' Roost.\n4\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Watchers' Roost\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. After arriving at Watchers' Roost, you have spotted Hermáth Stormhammer among the warriors of the Gabil'akkâ. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n",
[14120]="70015787\n1\tTalk to Búkk in Tharâkh Bazân\tBúkk can be found in Tharâkh Bazân, the gardens to the east. Kalman recommends that you speak with his friend Búkk about the mervyl.\n2\tTalk to Arnod in Tharâkh Bazân\tArnod can be found at the camp in Tharâkh Bazân, the gardens east of the Door to the Clouds. Búkk recommends speaking with Arnod, who has studied the maps and history of Khazad-dûm, about where to begin searching for mervyl.\n",
[14121]="70060013\n1\tInvestigate the frozen waters for Kúzun\tThe frozen waters Kúzun speaks of can found just west of Hlídborg in Câr Bronach. You should investigate the frozen waters for Kúzun.\n2\tInvestigate the icy pile\tThe frozen waters Kúzun speaks of can found just west of Hlídborg in Câr Bronach. You should investigate the frozen waters for Kúzun.\n3\tTalk to Kúzun at Leitstáth\tKúzun can be found at Leitstáth. You should talk to Kúzun.\n",
[14122]="7003FF47\n1\tSearch east of Alagrant for signs of fallen animals\tFallen animals can be found to the east of Alagrant, past where you discovered the fallen bear. Sarnir has asked you to examine more fallen animals on the fields of Blackroot Vale in hopes of discovering what has driven them to madness.\n2\tSearch further east for signs of fallen animals\tFallen animals can be found far to the east of Alagrant, near the Hill of Erech. You have found numerous animals mauled, but nothing that suggests anything unusual. You should continue your search to the east.\n3\tSearch the base of the Hill of Erech for fallen animals\tThe Hill of Erech can be found far to the east of Alagrant. You have discovered animals that appear to have been slain without a single wound. You should search for more felled beasts near the Hill of Erech.\n4\tTalk to Sarnir\tSarnir can be found in Alagrant in western Blackroot Vale. You have found evidence that the Dead at the Hill of Erech are responsible for the deaths of these creatures and you should now inform Sarnir.\n",
[14123]="70027179\n1\tBring the Nâkhmau symbol to Gwilum in Barnavon\tGwilum is at the gate to Lower Barnavon. You should bring the token you found to Gwilum.\n",
[14124]="70044D56\n1\tSearch the collection of enemy trophies for signs of thievery\tThe collection of enemy trophies can be found on the second floor of the Houses of Lore. Maenir has asked you to search the collection for signs of thievery before returning to him with the transcript of the stolen scroll.\n2\tCollect the scrawled transcript in the Houses of Lore\tThe scrawled transcript can be found among the collection of enemy trophies in the Houses of Lore. You have searched the collection and should now return to Maenir after collecting the transcript of the stolen scroll.\n3\tTalk to Maenir\tMaenir can be found on the first floor of the Houses of Lore in the Fifth Circle. You have searched the collection of enemy trophies and collected the transcript of the stolen scroll. You should now return to Maenir.\n4\tDeliver the scrawled transcript to Mithrandir\tMithrandir is in the Court of the Fountain on the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith. Maenir has asked you to seek Mithrandir's counsel in the hope that deciphering the content of the scroll might aid in capturing its thief.\n",
[14125]="700551E2\n1\tFind the old bathhouse in the Circle of Despair\030Defeat wailing Ithil-guards (total: 4)\tThe old bath-house can be found in the eastern reaches of the Circle of Despair. Wailing Ithil-guards can be found in the Circle of Despair. Dornach wants to investigate the old bath-house in the Circle of Despair. You should find the old bathhouse and defeat wailing Ithil-guards. NOTE: If you lose sight of Dornach, you can summon him to your side with his horn.\n2\tExplore the Gloomwaters\tThe old bath-house, now named the Gloomwaters, can be found in the eastern reaches of the Circle of Despair. Dornach wants to investigate the old bathhouse in the Circle of Despair. You should enter the old bathhouse. NOTE: If you lose sight of Dornach, you can summon him to your side with his horn.\n3\tExamine the glimmering brazier\tThe old bathhouse, now named the Gloomwaters, can be found in the eastern reaches of the Circle of Despair. You have entered the old bathhouse and discovered a glimmering brazier. You should examine it. NOTE: If you lose sight of Dornach, you can summon him to your side with his horn.\n4\tTalk to Dornach\tYou have put an end to the vile darkwater among the Dead of the Gloomwaters. You should talk to Dornach. NOTE: If you lose sight of Dornach, you can summon him to your side with his horn.\n",
[14126]="70015E1D\n1\tHelp Ruidhriel\030Help Limlaer\tRuidhriel is encamped near the Burnt Tor, north-west of Echad Dúnann. Limlaer is encamped along the road, south-west of Echad Dúnann. Rinneldor has asked you to speak with his scouts abroad, Ruidhriel and Limlaer, and aid them if you may.\n2\tTalk to Rinneldor at Echad Dúnann\tRinneldor is at Echad Dúnann, south-east of the Burnt Tor and north-east of Limlaer's post. You should return to Rinneldor and report all that you have learned regarding the Company's movements.\n",
[14127]="700272B5\n1\tDisable the traps intended to snare the cattle (total: 8)\tThe Dragon-clan set traps for the herd in the rocky fields on the west of the shallow river in the Herd-lands. You should disable the traps so that the herd may return without being brutally wounded for their loyalty.\n2\tTalk to Blodwen in the Herd-lands\tBlodwen is at her hiding place amid the rocks of Trum Dreng's southern farm, the Herd-lands. You should tell Blodwen that you have disabled all of the traps that you could find.\n",
[14128]="7000000C\n1\tTalk to Gammer Boffin\tGammer Boffin can be found at her home at the centre of Overhill. Shirriff Smallburrow has sent you to Overhill to speak with Gammer Boffin, an old hobbit with a great knowledge of herb-lore. Robin believes she might know of something to help clear the spider-webs away.\n2\tBring drams of slug-slime to Gammer Boffin\030Collect dram of slug-slime (total: 6)\tSlugs can be found in Rushock Bog, west of Overhill. Gammer Boffin is at her home in the middle of Overhill. Robin Smallburrow was sure that Gammer Boffin would know of some mixture that might help remove the webs blocking the spider-nest in Bindbole Wood. You went to Overhill and spoke with Gammer, who sent you to collect six drams of slug-slime.\n",
[14129]="70041472\n1\tSearch the Corsairs' cave\tThe Corsair hideout can be found in north-central Dor-en-Ernil along the mountainside. You have found slain Corsairs in their hideout and a sense of unease fills the air. You should investigate the cave further.\n2\tConfront the Ruthless Dead\tThe Ruthless oathbreaker can be found inside the Corsairs' cave in north-central Dor-en-Ernil. You have discovered the Ruthless Dead are behind the deaths of the Corsairs and should endeavour to discover their purpose in Dor-en-Ernil.\n3\tReturn to Garvir in Linhir\tGarvir can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil. You have discovered that the Ruthless Dead intend to sweep eastward through Lebennin towards Mordor and should bring these ill tidings to Garvir.\n",
[14130]="7002D413\n1\tFind the ancient shield in Uflûmp-mur\tUflûmp-mur can be found at the small outpost found at the entrance to Zirakzigil in Durin's Way. Listein has asked you to head east to Uflûmp-mur to find an ancient shield, so that he may learn what untold legends it holds.\n2\tReturn the shield to Listein at the entrance to Zirakzigil\tThe Door to the Clouds is just west of Uflûmp-mur, at the entrance to Zirakzigil in Durin's Way. You have found the ancient shield, and should return it to Listein for safe-keeping.\n",
[14131]="70026332\n1\tDefeat Angmarim in Annuminas (total: 40)\030Defeat Gertheryg in Annúminas (total: 10)\tAngmarim can be found within the bounds of the city of Annúminas. Orchalwë is desperate to defeat the Angmarim in Annúminas.\n2\tTalk to Orchalwë\tOrchalwë wants to speak to you.\n",
[14132]="70043B4A\n1\tTalk to Sabert at the east-gate of Stangard\tThe gate-keeper Sabert guards the eastern gate of Stangard, south of Haldirith. Bingo wants to do what he can to help relations between the Elves and the Rohirrim, and wants to travel south to Stangard.\n2\tTalk to Bingo outside the east-gate of Stangard\tBingo is outside the east-gate of Stangard, in Eorlsmead along the Great River. Sabert has rudely refused Bingo entrance to the outpost of Stangard.\n3\tSearch for the missing woman north-west of Stangard, near Frithstan's Camp in the Wailing Hills\tSabert turned a woman away from the gate of Stangard and now Bingo wants to search north-west of the outpost to find her and ensure her safety. Sabert thought she was headed in the direction of Frithstan's Camp.\n4\tTalk to Langhár outside Frithstan's Camp, in the Wailing Hills\tLanghár is outside Frithstan's Camp, in the Wailing Hills.\n5\tDefeat Orcs throughout the Wailing Hills (total: 12)\tOrcs can be found throughout the Wailing Hills. Langhár has asked you to help her defeat Orcs throughout the Wailing Hills, not really to aid the men of Stangard so much as to protect her home in the Vales of Anduin.\n6\tTalk to Bingo outside Frithstan's Camp, in the Wailing Hills\tBingo is outside Frithstan's Camp, in the Wailing Hills. You have defeated Orcs in the Wailing Hills, and should now return to Bingo and Langhár outside Frithstan's Camp.\n7\tTalk to Langhár outside Frithstan's Camp, in the Wailing Hills\tLanghár is outside Frithstan's Camp, in the Wailing Hills. You have defeated many Orcs in the Wailing Hills, and should now return to Langhár.\n8\tTalk to Landroval in the secluded clearing\tLanghár saw an Eagle descend into a stand of trees in the north-east corner of the Wailing Hills, on the edge of Thinglad, and thinks you should find him.\n9\tTalk to Bingo Boffin\tBingo Boffin is in a secluded clearing in the north-eastern corner of the Wailing Hills. You have found Landroval the Eagle, and Bingo seems to be quite overwhelmed by the great creature.\n10\tTalk to Langhár\tLanghár is in the secluded clearing in the north-east corner of the Wailing Hills.\n11\tCollect venom-sacs from spiders throughout the Wailing Hills (total: 8)\tLanghár thinks you should collect venom-sacs from spiders throughout the Wailing Hills, both in order to provide a helpful service and to give Bingo time to speak to Landroval.\n12\tYou have collected venom-sacs from the spiders of the Wailing Hills, and should return to the Secluded Clearing.\t\n13\tBingo is in the secluded clearing in the north-eastern corner of the Wailing Hills.\t\n14\tBring Landroval's warning to Sabert at the east-gate of Stangard\tSabert guards the east-gate of Stangard, and Bingo wants to warn him of the enemy presence Landroval saw gathering.\n15\tTalk to Bingo outside the east-gate of Stangard\tBingo is outside the east-gate of Stangard. Sabert did not heed your warning of an army in the Brown Lands.\n",
[14133]="7006AAC9\n1\tTravel to Ghâs Hejai to investigate the area\tBôgalekh has requested that you go to Ghâs Hejai to the north of Jadambor to investigate the Hakâri cultists.\n2\tGather any information you can from Hakâri cultists (total: 8)\tObtain any information you can from the Hakâri cultists that are gathered in Ghâs Hejai to the north of Jadambor.\n3\tInform Hênok of what you have discovered\tYou have gathered information regarding the Hakâri cultists and their plans. Bring what you have learned to Hênok located to the east of Ghâs Hejai.\n",
[14134]="70066925\n1\tDefeat Gelin warriors (total: 4)\030Defeat Gelin lobbers (total: 4)\030Gather woody mushrooms (total: 8)\tDerva has asked you to defeat wood-trolls and pick mushrooms. Wood-trolls and the mushrooms she seeks can be found in the woods to the north-west.\n2\tTalk to Derva\t\n",
[14135]="700397E8\n1\tRescue crofters from the Dunlendings\tYou have encountered crofters bound inside their own farmhouse. You should rescue them from the nearby Dunlendings. Crofters can be found inside the homestead to the south-east of Middlemead.\n2\tCaptured crofters can be found inside the homestead to the south-east of Middlemead. You have come across crofters captured by Dunlendings. You should free them from their captors and aid in reclaiming their homestead.\t\n3\tCompleted\tYou have freed all of the crofters from their captors and brought some measure of peace back to the homestead.\n",
[14136]="70052942\n1\tDefeat spiders in the woods of Laerlad (total: 12)\tSpiders can be found in the woods of Laerlad. You should defeat spiders in the woods of Laerlad.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many spiders in the woods of Laerlad.\n",
[14137]="7004DA49\n1\tRemove angry scrawls (total: 7)\tYou should find angry scrawls on walls and doors throughout Dale and remove them.\n2\tTalk to Gaumar\tYou should return to Gaumar.\n",
[14138]="700005C2\n1\tDeliver the produce to Wilmac Brandybuck\030Collect Farmer Maggot's produce\tThe brigands' stockade is north of the road, between the Brandywine Bridge and Adso's camp. Wilmac Brandybuck awaits you inside the Hay Gate in Newbury, Buckland. Wilmac Brandybuck has asked you to retrieve Farmer Maggot's produce from the ruffians who accosted him.\n",
[14139]="7002D546\n1\tDefeat deep-claws (total: 10)\030Destroy filthy nests (total: 6)\tThe nest of deep-claws can be found in the Old Silvertine City in the southern Silvertine Lodes. You should defeat deep-claws and clean up the nest area.\n2\tTalk to Öndótt\tÖndótt can be found at the top of the stair in the Old Silvertine City. You should return to Öndótt and tell him that you have done as he asked.\n",
[14140]="7005F6C5\n1\tRescue Longbeard guards from webs in Glittengrof (total: 8)\tWriggling webs can be found in Glittengrof. Vithin has asked you to aid in the rescue of several Longbeard guards who were captured by the glass-spiders now dwelling in Glittengrof. You should rescue the Longbeard guards.\n2\tTalk to Vithin in Glittengrof\tVithin can be found in Glittengrof in Gloomingtarn. You have successfully rescued all of the Longbeard guards captured by the glass-spiders. You should return to Vithin.\n",
[14141]="7000781B\n1\tTalk to Lily Underhill at her farm\tLily Underhill's home is east of the town square, past Boggs' Farm. Longo Daegmund, worried about the Staddle town-well, asked you to speak with Lily Underhill.\n",
[14142]="70024BD1\n1\tCollect firewood from the best trees (total: 9)\tGrouchy trees can be chopped down in the woods in the Grumpwood, a forbidding forest in the northern-most reaches of Frostbluff. You should use whatever force is necessary to get firewood from only the best trees.\n2\tBring the hardy firewood to Mabel Mitford\tMabel Mitford is in Winter-home. You should bring the firewood you gathered to Mabel Mitford.\n",
[14143]="70003799\n1\tCollect relic-fragments\tSnow-lurkers climb the drifts near the source of the Bruinen in the Misty Mountains north of Rivendell. As the creatures make their way through the snow, shards of pottery and old relics become tangled in their root-like legs. Collect relic fragments from snow lurkers in the Misty Mountains.\n2\tCollect relic-fragments (total: 4)\tSnow-lurkers climb the drifts near the source of the Bruinen in the Misty Mountains north of Rivendell. As the creatures make their way through the snow, shards of pottery and old relics become tangled in their root-like legs. Collect relic fragments from snow lurkers in the Misty Mountains.\n3\tBring relic fragments to Glorenglir in Rivendell\tGlorenglir is interested in investigating these relic fragments collected from the Misty Mountains. Glorenglir may be found in Rivendell.\n",
[14144]="70042F5D\n1\tSearch for Echil in the High Archives\tEchil is somewhere inside the High Archives in western Osgiliath. Candúr has asked you to seek his lost fellow, Echil, and then recover any valuable writings that survived the sack of western Osgiliath.\n2\tCollect bundles of recovered writings (total: 6)\030Collect crumbling tomes carefully (total: 3)\tRecovered writings and crumbling tomes can be found inside the High Archives in western Osgiliath. You have found Echil and should now search for recovered writings and valuable tomes before returning to Candúr.\n3\tTalk to Candúr\tCandúr can be found just outside the High Archives in western Osgiliath. You have found Echil and recovered many valuable pieces of writing from the High Archives. You should now return to Candúr.\n",
})
